&lt;p&gt;FEQ427R388&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As an Senior Manager, Field Engineering, you will lead a broader team of technical customer advisors and help shape the strategy, roadmap, and operating model for a significant Field Engineering portfolio. You will scale impact beyond your immediate team through other leaders, cross-functional initiatives, reusable practices, and strong customer and partner relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role typically leads Field Engineering professionals across a broader portfolio and may include responsibility for one or two managers. Depending on the assignment, you may support a major segment, a multi-country portfolio, or an equivalent area of complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;THE IMPACT YOU WILL HAVE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop Field Engineering professionals and emerging people leaders across a broader portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team strategy and roadmaps that connect customer needs, technical priorities, business outcomes, and broader Field Engineering goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasingly influence the most important priorities for the portfolio and help teams see around corners over the next 3–6–12 months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and cross-functional leadership to shape technical-win strategy, resource allocation, customer coverage, and execution plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with senior customer stakeholders and use customer, market, and competitive insight to improve account and portfolio strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable inspection mechanisms across teams, including portfolio reviews, customer-health reviews, technical-risk reviews, and escalation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach leaders and senior practitioners through complex customer, technical, competitive, organizational, and performance situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and share playbooks, tools, enablement, and operating mechanisms that increase productivity and consistency beyond one team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence Product, Engineering, Support, Professional Services, Marketing, and Partners on customer requirements, product gaps, and cross-functional priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and automation to create one-to-many impact across enablement, execution, forecasting, customer planning, and team productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model and strengthen a culture of psychological safety, inclusion, accountability, continuous learning, and high performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WHAT WE LOOK FOR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading technical customer-facing teams in enterprise software, cloud, data, AI, analytics, technical consulting, or a related environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to hire bar-raising talent, develop leaders, manage performance, and make thoughtful decisions about team structure, capability mix, and resourcing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading through other leaders or serving as a senior leader on a complex team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgment: you can identify the highest-impact priorities, allocate resources, manage risk, and connect near-term execution to longer-term goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building repeatable operating mechanisms, playbooks, tools, or programs that scale beyond your immediate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence senior internal partners across Sales, Professional Services, Solutions Architecture, Marketing, Partners, Product, Engineering, and Support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer-advisory capability, including the ability to guide senior stakeholders through complex technical and business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient understanding of data and AI technologies, cloud architecture, governance, security, networking, and enterprise adoption considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-first, builder mindset with evidence of applying emerging tools or approaches to improve customer outcomes and organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated alignment with Databricks Culture Principles and the ability to translate them into clear expectations and daily team practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing technical customer-facing teams and/or other people leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder customer engagements and cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data platforms, analytics, AI, cloud, software, technical consulting, or a related technical domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written, verbal, presentation, decision-making, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks or comparable data and AI platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading across multiple segments, geographies, countries, customer portfolios, or technical practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or improving Field Engineering, Solutions Architecture, technical sales, customer success, or similar operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building partner ecosystems and cross-functional communities of practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI, automation, dashboards, or other mechanisms to improve organizational scale and repeatability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
